The top-level help. **Every line below is contract**, byte for byte — no wildcards, so any change
to the surface shows up as a diff a reviewer has to agree to.

```
$ renvor --help
Create and run Renvor projects.

Exit codes: 0 success, 1 internal defect, 2 usage, 3 validation, 4 cancelled, 5 environment.

Usage: renvor[EXE] [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  new     Create a project, from prompts or from flags
  doctor  Report environment readiness
  check   Validate a project without building it
  routes  Show the routes this project would serve
  dev     Run the local development loop
  docker  Container development controls
  tls     Local TLS trust. Issues no certificate and modifies no trust store in this phase

Options:
      --output <human|json>
          Result format for stdout
          
          [default: human]

      --yes
          Accept confirmations. Never waives validation

      --dry-run
          Compute and report without writing anything

      --no-color
          Disable styling. Styling is also off automatically when the stream is not a terminal

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

```
